DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The login accounting service module for PAM, ppaamm__llaassttlloogg provides func‐
     tionality for only one PAM category: session management.  In terms of the
     _m_o_d_u_l_e_-_t_y_p_e parameter, this is the “session” feature.

   LLooggiinn AAccccoouunnttiinngg SSeessssiioonn MMaannaaggeemmeenntt MMoodduullee
     The login accounting session management component provides functions to
     initiate (ppaamm__ssmm__ooppeenn__sseessssiioonn()) and terminate (ppaamm__ssmm__cclloossee__sseessssiioonn())
     sessions.  The ppaamm__ssmm__ooppeenn__sseessssiioonn() function records the session in the
     user accounting database.  The ppaamm__ssmm__cclloossee__sseessssiioonn() function does noth‐
     ing.

     The following options may be passed to the authentication module:

     ddeebbuugg    syslog(3) debugging information at LOG_DEBUG level.

     nnoo__wwaarrnn  suppress warning messages to the user.

     nnoo__ffaaiill  Ignore I/O failures.

